## 4. Kenya statutory checklist

Keep every figure in `rate_versions`. Verify current rates and thresholds against KRA, NSSF, SHA and the Finance Act before each release. Values below are for orientation only.

| Item | What the system must do |
| --- | --- |
| **PAYE** | Progressive bands on taxable pay; personal relief; insurance relief; owner-occupied interest; pension/retirement contribution; post-retirement medical; disability exemption; consultants at withholding rates |
| **NSSF** | Tier I and II, employee and employer, lower/upper earnings limits that step up by year; exempt/contracted-out cases |
| **SHIF (SHA)** | Percentage of gross with a minimum; employee only; deductible from taxable pay |
| **Affordable Housing Levy** | Employee and employer percentage of gross; deductible from taxable pay; remit via iTax |
| **NITA** | Flat monthly amount per employee, employer-paid |
| **WIBA** | Employer insurance cover; keep policy details per company |
| **Fringe benefits** | Low-interest loans, company car, housing; taxable benefit computed per rules |
| **Overtime** | Normal-day and rest/holiday-day multipliers per Employment Act and wage orders |
| **Leave** | Annual, sick (full then half pay), maternity, paternity, compassionate; carry-over by policy |
| **Termination** | Notice, service pay (per completed year where no NSSF/pension), severance on redundancy, certificate of service |
| **Regulation of Wages orders** | Minimum wage by sector and location: hospitality-first product should warn when basic is below minimum |
| **Service charge** | Hotels/restaurants: pooled and distributed per employment rules, shown on payslip |
| **Data Protection Act 2019** | Consent and purpose for personal data; access/correction by employee; ODPC registration for the controller; retention rules; no salary or ID data in logs |
| **Records** | Keep payroll records at least 7 years (KRA); 3 years minimum under Employment Act; archive, never delete |

